# This repo is authored on ext4 under WSL and cloned on Windows too -- step 1
# of the install runs .\windows\bootstrap.ps1 from a host checkout. That second
# copy is the whole reason this file exists.
#
# Git for Windows ships core.autocrlf=true in its system gitconfig
# (C:/Program Files/Git/etc/gitconfig), which converts on the way in and out
# using a heuristic about what counts as text. The heuristic is usually right,
# and "usually right" is not a property a shell script can rely on: a .sh that
# reaches Ubuntu with CRLF fails at the shebang with
#   bad interpreter: /usr/bin/env bash^M
# which names neither the file nor the real cause.
#
# Declaring it here removes the machine from the answer. The repo stores LF and
# checks out LF everywhere, whatever any clone has autocrlf set to.
* text=auto eol=lf

# .ps1 is included in the rule above on purpose rather than exempted: both
# Windows PowerShell 5.1 and PowerShell 7 read LF scripts without complaint,
# and an exemption here would be the one file able to reintroduce CRLF.

# Binary, so no conversion is attempted and no diff is produced.
*.png binary
*.zip binary
*.ttf binary
